he fixture placed the item into its own zone. The\nhonest version was then run: pemmican dropped 25+ cells from any zone,\nunforbidden, and 8,000 REAL ticks advanced — **vanilla haul jobs moved it\ninto zone b specifically** (the Important, Foods-only zone — the game's own\npriority system choosing the fixture's configuration), and\n`by_location`/`in:stockpile`/per-thing detail all tracked the transition\nmid-haul (90 arrived, the rest in transit). `stockpiled` follows the game's\nbehaviour, not our arrangement.\n\n**Met in weaker form, in those words:** the opaque-window tier (tier 3) was\nnever exercised against a live modded window — no shipped verb opens one and\ndriving mod UI by hand is not in this harness. It is safe BY CONSTRUCTION\n(fields only, never properties — a field read cannot execute game code) and\ncode-reviewed; the first Hospitality/Storefront window a real run meets will\nbe its live test. `in:room`/`in:rect` scopes and `things detail` HP/quality\nedge fields were exercised lightly (detail ran; per-field cross-checks were\ndef-level).\n\n**Zero red errors** across both sessions; journal seq gaps zero; Player.log\n0 exceptions.\n\n**Knock-on fixes landed with this merge (orchestrator commits):** 2.3's\nmap-view no longer trips the growing-zone scribed write (CropRenderer now\nreads WorldSafe.PlantToGrow — shipped code was writing the save on every\nmap-view over an unconfigured zone); the digest sees fire map-wide; DESIGN's\ndecisions log records the observer gate-in-the-widget rule with the four\nbanned accessors; README's git-bug trap list corrected per this worker's\nfinding (# lines are dropped AT STORAGE, not merely in show — measured, and\nit had already cost this session a mistitled issue).","files":null}]}